  "source": "servicer policy LM-2 (summary of the loss mitigation rule)",
  "actor": "Saltmarsh Home Loans",
  "entry": "1) If an application is received 45 or more days before a scheduled sale, send a written acknowledgment within 5 days (excluding weekends and legal holidays) stating whether it is complete and listing missing documents. 2) If a complete application is received more than 37 days before a scheduled sale, evaluate it within 30 days and send a written decision. 3) The borrower may accept or reject an offer within 14 days if the complete application was received 90 or more days before the sale, or within 7 days if received fewer than 90 but more than 37 days before the sale; a borrower who does not respond by the deadline is treated as having rejected the offer. 4) An appeal of a denial is available only if the complete application was received 90 or more days before the sale. 5) If a complete application was received more than 37 days before the sale, the sale may not be held unless the borrower was denied for all options (and any appeal is finished or unavailable), the borrower rejected all options offered, or the borrower failed to perform under an agreement."
 },
